    "narrative": "Our strongest play for today\u2019s slate is **Isaac Paredes**, who commands an elite score of 72.13. Facing an extremely favorable matchup against Klassen (xERA 6.12), **Isaac Paredes** benefits from an immense SP skill edge (+19%) and a dynamic platoon advantage (+9%), making him the clear anchor for the lineup. Following closely is **Corbin Carroll**, whose 66.31 score is driven by his elite SB potential; even against the tough Suarez (xERA 3.65), **Corbin Carroll** gains a +4% efficiency boost from the starter's slow delivery, which we expect to exploit on the basepaths. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** (62.06) is a high-conviction start, buoyed by a +8% order bonus and a +5% wind-out factor, alongside his own favorable profile against Hudson\u2019s slow delivery.\n\nThe most difficult decision on our bench was **Vinnie Pasquantino**, who landed at a 43.58 score. While **Vinnie Pasquantino** is a staple for our core, he narrowly missed the starting cut due to a -15% dynamic platoon penalty against Basso, which suppressed his efficiency below our current 1B and UTIL options. We remain cautious with **Mickey Moniak**, whose 65.81 projection is admittedly strong, but his 37% rain risk makes him a volatility play; should the weather turn, we have limited flexibility to swap him out. Finally, we must note the absence of **James Wood**, who remains on the IL, further tightening our depth and reinforcing the necessity of relying on the speed-oriented ceiling provided by **Brice Turang** and **Henry Bolte** today.",
